@startuml cad-handoff
!include theme.iuml
title CAD wrapper — transfer files without changing the evaluator contract
autonumber

box "CAD session container + persistent workspace" #EAF2F8
  participant "CAD agent" as Agent
  participant "Local MCP adapter" as MCP
end box
participant "Backend + dispatcher\ndurable operation / attempt state" as App
database "Scoped immutable storage" as Store
participant "Isolated FreeCAD attempt\nM-CAD local file contract" as Core #F9E4E2

Agent -> MCP : asset_fetch(asset_id), if an input is needed
MCP -> App : authorized asset retrieval
App -> Store : read immutable bytes
Store --> App : bytes + digest
App --> MCP : bytes + digest
MCP --> Agent : completed file in this session's workspace

Agent -> Agent : write model.py + request.json + declared inputs
Agent -> MCP : cad_evaluate(request_path, idempotency_key)
MCP -> MCP : validate allowed paths; snapshot completed local files
MCP -> App : input bundle bytes + relative manifest + idempotency key
App -> Store : finalize frozen input bundle
App -> App : accept operation once; persist task / session context
App --> MCP : operation_id + accepted status
MCP --> Agent : operation_id for status / bounded wait

App -> Core : materialize declared files; route to CLI or retained runtime;\nevaluate with private query output directory
note over MCP, Core
  A source path is meaningful only where its bytes live.
  Transfer bytes; preserve relative request paths and digests.
  Runtime/mount authority belongs to the dispatcher, never submitted code.
end note
Core -> Core : ensure / reuse geometry -> requested evidence -> result.json
Core --> App : query completion + finalized files, or interrupted attempt;\nretained runtime stays alive
App -> App : verify paths / digests / attempt ownership / cancellation
App -> Store : capture completed evidence; record outer operation outcome

Agent -> MCP : cad_status / bounded cad_wait(operation_id)
MCP -> App : retrieve state + completed result bundle
App --> MCP : result.json + completed files + digests
MCP -> MCP : materialize bundle atomically in session-local run directory
MCP --> Agent : operation/run IDs + local result / artifact paths

Agent -> Agent : inspect files; revise code or return evidence
opt explicit user-visible publication
  Agent -> MCP : result_publish(selected local files, run_id, idempotency_key,\nmessage_mode: together / per_image)
  MCP -> App : submit completed bytes + verified provenance
  App -> Store : finalize immutable selected assets
  App -> App : commit result manifest + ordered message identities once
  App --> MCP : durable result / asset references
  MCP --> Agent : durable result / asset references
end

note over Agent, App
  Another agent receives stored references and fetches its own local copies.
  Grid / separate images / both; deliver together or per image with the same result reference.
  One MCP result can describe several images and chat messages (CAD-PROTOCOL-13).
  Preserve JSON sidecars and inline labels together (CAD-PROTOCOL-14).
  Scoped live geometry handles route to retained state; snapshot restore does not run source (CAD-PROTOCOL-15).
  Retry and recovery use durable operation/attempt IDs; the core remains file based.
  Stop fences stale capture/publication and stops the owned attempt process tree.
end note

legend bottom
  Review draft: docs/architecture/CAD-PROTOCOL.md. M-CAD.md owns the inner contract.
  Storing an evaluation is distinct from publishing selected results in chat.
  ACP session recovery is background context, shown separately in sessions / acp-turn.
endlegend
@enduml
